div.p:
In the West German sources, biology and reproduction dominate discussions of sexuality. That is, in keeping with the authors’ disciplinary backgrounds, sex is discussed in almost exclusively anatomical and reproductive terms. They portrayed women’s sexuality, furthermore, as passive and centred on procreation. Thus Husslein, for instance, says that

 for the emotionally (

  seelisch

 ) mature young woman, love culminates in the wish to symbolize the union in a child,… [a] wish most strongly felt during sex,

and that

 a woman deceives herself when she seeks only sexual satisfaction from the bodily union and bans from her world of feeling everything that has to do with motherhood and love of child (

  Liebe zum Kind

 ).


 81
